  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    (f : ℝ → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let μ : (n : ℕ) → Measure (Fin n → Bool) := fun n =>\n      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count\n    let S : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ := fun n ε =>\n      (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1\n    let γ : Measure ℝ := gaussianReal 0 1\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2) γ ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) γ ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => (deriv f x)^2) γ ∧\n    (∀ n : ℕ,\n      Integrable (fun ε => (f (S n ε))^2) (μ n) ∧\n      Integrable (fun ε => (f (S n ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S n ε))^2)) (μ n) ∧\n      Integrable (fun ε => (deriv f (S n ε))^2) (μ n)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop\n      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ∫ ε,\n      (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) atTop\n      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ∫ ε, (deriv f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop\n      (𝓝 (∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =>\n      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) -\n      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) *\n        Real.log (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1))) atTop\n      (𝓝 ((∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -\n        (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ)))",
    "statement_sha256": "ded6876a5ef31561123243e3e9692489ba2a3633a396fe27e478ae8e6825b6c3",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "All functions and derivatives are on the real line with its canonical Borel structure. ContDiff Real 2 f means C2, and HasCompactSupport f means the closure of the nonzero support is compact. deriv is the real derivative; C2 supplies differentiability.",
      "For each n, Fin n -> Bool is the actual finite carrier, with canonical finite measurable structure. mu is counting measure scaled by inverse actual carrier cardinal in ENNReal. S is the displayed actual signed sum: true1, false-1, divided by sqrt(n); inverse0=0 and Fin0 sum is empty.",
      "gamma=gaussianReal0 1 is the real probability Gaussian of mean0 and varianceNNReal1. Integrable is actual Bochner integrability for the specified measure; the displayed integrals are Bochner integrals.",
      "Real.log is totalized at zero by log0=0. The displayed entropy is integral f²log(f²) minus mass times log(mass), including zero mass. Tendsto atTop into nhdsReal denotes real scalar convergence of the displayed successor integrals.",
      "Only f and its C2/compact-support assumptions are caller inputs. Every displayed Gaussian or finite-count integrability fact and every displayed limit is a conclusion; no law, limit, positivity, integrability, or entropy certificate is supplied."
    ]
